Downstream attribution
----------------------
When a public product, service, distribution, device, or system incorporates
OpenXTOS or an OpenXTOS component, the distributor should provide a clear
attribution in the product's About, system-information, open-source notices,
or equivalent screen and in the accompanying documentation where practical.
The attribution should identify:

  OpenXTOS / XTOS
  upstream version and, where available, source commit
  https://xtos.cn
  the downstream distributor
  whether the downstream work has been modified

Suggested wording:

  Based on OpenXTOS 0.9.0 (source commit
  dd313955ad57542bcd2af8827157d1bbd0cf5e83).
  Project: https://xtos.cn
  Distributed by: [downstream distributor].
  Modifications: [brief description or "none"]

This notice is an attribution guide. It does not modify the software licenses
and does not replace, narrow, or add conditions to the applicable Apache-2.0
or GPL-2.0 license. It does not grant
permission to imply that a downstream product is official, certified, or
